cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "opportunity-engine: finding and winning paid work from free sources, for a market screened by machines"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Seyedkazemi Ardebili"
    given-names: "Mohsen"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1166-6559"
    website: "https://mskazemi.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/opportunity-engine"
url: "https://github.com/MSKazemi/opportunity-engine"
abstract: >-
  opportunity-engine finds, ranks and helps win paid work of any shape — employment,
  contract, freelance projects, fellowships and collaborations — using only sources
  that are usable with no payment. It stores opportunities in schema.org/JobPosting
  shape and the candidate profile as JSON Resume, on the premise that hiring is now
  screened by two machines in sequence (a parsing layer and a language-model ranking
  layer) and that machine-legible, verifiable evidence is the interface. Every source
  in its registry records how and when it was verified, and the tool never fabricates
  a field it cannot fill truthfully from the user's own profile.
keywords:
  - job-search
  - freelance
  - applicant-tracking-system
  - ats
  - json-resume
  - schema-org
  - automation
  - cli
